                                "text": "As a matter of fact these chapters coincide pretty closely with the Book of the Laws of Countries extant in Syriac and in part in Greek, written by an early Bardesanist ; and comparison shows that the Recognitions borrowed from the Bardesanist Book , not vice versâ ”"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "aba91fb9-5843-4f2b-ba65-cb94a3c2a309",
                                "sense_id": "57fe23d6-4964-3b46-91ed-24fccfea06ca",
                                "text": "No doubt Bardaisan, or his son Harmonius, or whatever Bardesanist wrote the poem, was familiar with the great caravan route from India to Egypt, and used this knowledge as a substructure, but the whole is allegorical."
